 "mod-2.tagline": "Follow the packet from the browser to the application process.",
 "mod-2.overview": "Almost every production incident is, at its core, a path problem: DNS pointing to the wrong place, a blocked port, an expired certificate, a downed upstream. In this module you learn to trace that path with tools — dig, curl, ss, tcpdump — and to operate Nginx as a reverse proxy, truly understanding the difference between 502, 503 and 504.",
 "mod-2.objectives": "Explain IP, subnet, gateway, and routes | Diagnose DNS by record, TTL, and queried server | Read HTTP/HTTPS requests with curl and interpret status and headers | Configure Nginx as a reverse proxy with TLS | Differentiate and resolve 502, 503, and 504",
 "mod-2.prerequisites": "Module 1 completed",
 "mod-2.delivery": "API with /health endpoint published behind Nginx with TLS, plus a 502/503/504 diagnostic document.",
 "mod-2.checklist": "dig of the domain returns the expected IP and you know the TTL | curl -I on the domain returns 200 via HTTPS | Nginx correctly forwards X-Forwarded-For and Host headers | Proxy timeouts adjusted and documented | Firewall opening only 22, 80, and 443",
 "mod-2.troubleshooting": "Symptom: users receive intermittent 502. Investigation: Nginx error log shows 'connect() failed (111: Connection refused)' — meaning the upstream is not accepting connections. Confirmation: curl on the direct upstream and ss -tulpn on the API host. Root cause: the API restarted due to out of memory. Correction: memory limit, automatic restart, and readiness before receiving traffic.",
 "mod-2.interviewQuestions": "What's the difference between 502, 503, and 504, and what does each say about the backend? | How do you check if a problem is DNS, network, or application? | What happens in the TLS handshake and why does an expired certificate break everything?",
 "mod-2.capstone": "Publish the CloudShop API at api.cloudshop.dev behind Nginx with HTTPS.",
 "l-2-1.title": "IP, subnets, ports and the path of the packet",
