 "mod-3.title": "Git, GitHub and Bash",
 "mod-3.tagline": "Collaborate without breaking main and automate the repetitive.",
 "mod-3.overview": "Git is the foundation of CI/CD and GitOps: without clean history and a predictable flow, automation isn't reliable. You'll master branches, PRs, merge versus rebase, revert, tags and releases, plus protecting main with rules. In the second half, Bash: idempotent scripts with error handling that replace manual tasks like health-checks and log backups.",
 "mod-3.objectives": "Work with branches and Pull Requests professionally | Choose between merge, rebase, and revert consciously | Publish releases with semantic tags | Write secure Bash scripts with set -euo pipefail | Protect the main branch with rules and mandatory checks",
