 "mod-3.delivery": "Health-check and log backup scripts in Bash, with main protected requiring review and green CI.",
 "mod-3.checklist": "Main protected: no direct push, PR with approval and status check | Merge conflict manually resolved and documented | Tag v1.0.0 published with release notes | Script with set -euo pipefail, trap and correct exit code | Compressed log backup with defined retention",
 "mod-3.troubleshooting": "Symptom: A bad commit is already in main and in production. Options: revert (creates a commit that undoes, safe in shared branch) or reset (rewrites history, forbidden in shared branch). Correct decision: git revert, deploy the new version, and a short postmortem explaining why CI didn't catch it.",
 "mod-3.interviewQuestions": "When do you use rebase and when do you use merge? | How to revert something already published without rewriting history? | What does set -euo pipefail do and why is it mandatory in automation scripts?",
 "mod-3.capstone": "Protect the cloudshop-app repository and automate verification and backup on the host.",
 "l-3-1.title": "Branches, commits and Pull Requests that pass review",
 "l-3-1.objectives": "Adopt a simple branching flow | Write clear commits and PRs | Configure main branch protection",
 "l-3-1.whyItMatters": "Pipelines, GitOps, and rollbacks depend on a predictable history. A chaotic repository contaminates all automation.",
 "l-3-1.commonMistake": "Committing everything in a single giant commit with the message 'adjustments'.",
 "l-3-1.productionTip": "Squash merge keeps main clean and facilitates reverting an entire change.",
 "l-3-1.securityAlert": "Enable secret scanning in the repository; a committed token must be revoked, not just removed.",
 "l-3-1.interviewQuestion": "How would you organize the branch workflow for a team of five people?",
 "l-3-1.capstone": "Open the PR for the /health endpoint in cloudshop-app with mandatory CI.",
 "l-3-1.q0": "Which practice reduces merge conflicts?",
 "l-3-1.q0opts": "Long-lived branches | Integrate frequently with short-lived branches | Avoid PRs | Commit only at the end of the month",
 "l-3-1.q0exp": "The smaller the divergence between the branch and main, the lower the chance of conflict.",
 "l-3-2.title": "Merge, rebase, revert: rewriting or preserving history",
 "l-3-2.objectives": "Resolve conflicts safely | Apply rebase only where it's safe | Revert published changes",
