 "devsecops.name": "DevSecOps",
 "interview.0.id": "iq-1",
 "interview.0.area": "Linux",
 "interview.1.id": "iq-2",
 "interview.1.strongAnswer": "502: the proxy tried and the upstream refused or closed the connection — usually a crashed process or wrong port. 503: no upstream available or the proxy itself is rate-limiting. 504: the upstream accepted but exceeded the read timeout — usually a slow query. The proof is in the error.log and in testing the upstream directly with curl.",
 "interview.2.id": "iq-3",
 "interview.2.area": "Containers",
 "interview.2.strongAnswer": "The container lives as long as the main process lives. If the command finishes — successfully or with an error — the container stops. I diagnose with docker logs, check entrypoint/cmd and environment variables, and confirm if the process is in the foreground.",
 "interview.3.id": "iq-4",
 "interview.3.area": "CI/CD",
 "interview.3.strongAnswer": "I use OIDC: the workflow requests an identity token and assumes a restricted role per repository and ref in the trust policy. There's no key to leak or rotate, and the role limits exactly the allowed actions. I also declare minimum permissions in the workflow.",
 "interview.4.id": "iq-5",
 "interview.4.area": "Cloud",
 "interview.4.strongAnswer": "A public subnet is one whose route table points 0.0.0.0/0 to the Internet Gateway. A database in a private subnet, with a Security Group accepting only the application's SG, eliminates direct internet exposure. Outbound access, when necessary, goes through NAT or a VPC endpoint.",
 "interview.5.id": "iq-6",
 "interview.5.area": "IaC",
 "interview.5.strongAnswer": "Drift is a divergence between code and reality, usually due to manual changes during an incident. I detect it with a scheduled plan using -detailed-exitcode. I don't apply before understanding: legitimate differences go into the code (or are imported), accidental ones are reverted by the apply. And the team's rule is that manual fixes become a PR on the same day.",
 "interview.6.id": "iq-7",
 "interview.6.area": "Kubernetes",
